This new strategy aims to dynamically adjust interventions based on the current system state, balancing between corrective actions and minimal adjustments to maintain stability without inducing unnecessary oscillations. Continuous evaluation and adaptation of this strategy will be crucial to achieving optimal performance in keeping the pole balanced for longer durations.
